      "effective_date": "2025-06-27",
      "verification": "not_recorded",
      "verification_note": "KRS 141.020 confirms the flat rates by year. It does not state the standard deduction. The 2024 e-file handbook (https://revenue.ky.gov/Documents/TY2024%20E-File%20HandBook%20Publication%201345_v1.0.pdf, sha256 ff1518fdfb27eeac42f780fef0a727dc4d7d359866da6cf0b60dee5eabca850a, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction increased from $2,980 to $3,160 for tax year 2024, so the held $3,160 is not the 2023 deduction. A year before 2025 still uses $3,160. The 2025 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Packet%20Instructions.pdf, sha256 cdb8e571c09f306961d5cb62154f8b57bd67f6ee50376b443647376b5667f421, retrieved 2026-11-10) states a 4% rate and a $3,270 standard deduction. The 2026 withholding formula (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/2026%20Withholding%20Formula.pdf, sha256 3876018d7019cf2b8ffae40554376ef2e6900809221517c26d8e71e025f5e439, retrieved 2026-11-10) states a 3.5% rate and a $3,360 standard deduction. The September 4, 2025 DOR announcement (https://revenue.ky.gov/News/Pages/Kentucky-DOR-Announces-2026-Standard-Deduction.aspx, sha256 f058b78a07a43e541838fd35a2b991f90e70a1d50e7cd4fcaf1ac1d994875416, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the 2026 standard deduction is $3,360.",
